  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "6655772",
      "title": "Fully Understanding the Component Selector",
      "lectureOrder": 344,
      "videoOrder": 321,
      "sourceHash": "a887baf1303f174676f9937816843fb75e7055473edc06da1175cfcc3ddddd4c",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.61,
          "end": 5.52,
          "en": "-: Now are you already a component ninja?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.52,
          "end": 7.17,
          "en": "We learned a lot about components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.17,
          "end": 9.84,
          "en": "about the templates, options we have there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.84,
          "end": 11.283,
          "en": "and about the styles.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.45,
          "end": 15.24,
          "en": "I want to focus on the last property we see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.24,
          "end": 19.71,
          "en": "in this component decorator for now, the selector.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.71,
          "end": 23.85,
          "en": "I already mentioned that this has to be a unique selector",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.85,
          "end": 27.06,
          "en": "so that you don't overwrite accidentally an already",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.06,
          "end": 31.74,
          "en": "existing element or maybe a component made available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.74,
          "end": 34.533,
          "en": "by another third party package you use in your project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.67,
          "end": 37.08,
          "en": "There's one other piece of information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.08,
          "end": 38.7,
          "en": "about the selector though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.7,
          "end": 43.29,
          "en": "You don't have to use this type of selector.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.29,
          "end": 47.13,
          "en": "Right now, our selector is the same selector",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 47.13,
          "end": 51.63,
          "en": "as we use it in css for selecting a element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.63,
          "end": 54.66,
          "en": "So we have app servers here as a element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 54.66,
          "end": 58.53,
          "en": "and this is recognized by Angular because the selector",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 58.53,
          "end": 60.99,
          "en": "which shows is app servers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 60.99,
          "end": 62.43,
          "en": "And this basically just looks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 62.43,
          "end": 65.37,
          "en": "how you select elements in css, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 65.37,
          "end": 67.56,
          "en": "We select the h3 element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 67.56,
          "end": 69.96000000000001,
          "en": "by just typing h3 here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.96000000000001,
          "end": 73.95,
          "en": "We select the app servers element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.95,
          "end": 77.7,
          "en": "by just typing app servers here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 77.7,
          "end": 81.48,
          "en": "So that actually works like a css selector",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 81.48,
          "end": 86.48,
          "en": "and therefore you are not limited to selecting by element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 87.03,
          "end": 90.78,
          "en": "You could put this into square brackets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 90.78,
          "end": 93.57,
          "en": "to use the attribute selector.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 93.57,
          "end": 96.03,
          "en": "So in css you can select elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 96.03,
          "end": 98.58,
          "en": "by attribute, by enclosing that attribute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 98.58,
          "end": 100.25999999999999,
          "en": "in square brackets.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 100.25999999999999,
          "end": 102.6,
          "en": "And now if you save this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 102.6,
          "end": 106.8,
          "en": "you would see that our app actually is broken.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 106.8,
          "end": 109.2,
          "en": "Because if we have a look at the error message,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 109.2,
          "end": 113.72999999999999,
          "en": "app servers is a unknown element because now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 113.72999999999999,
          "end": 118.28999999999999,
          "en": "our code Angular doesn't recognize app servers anymore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 118.28999999999999,
          "end": 122.25,
          "en": "because we changed the selector to be an attribute.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 122.25,
          "end": 123.78,
          "en": "So to make this work again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 123.78,
          "end": 125.16,
          "en": "we would have to comment this out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 125.16,
          "end": 127.62,
          "en": "or remove it and maybe add a div",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 127.62,
          "end": 130.559,
          "en": "or any other element, a normal HTML element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 130.559,
          "end": 135,
          "en": "which has a app servers attribute now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 135,
          "end": 138.18,
          "en": "Now with this custom attribute added now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 138.18,
          "end": 139.59,
          "en": "now the app works again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 139.59,
          "end": 142.38,
          "en": "because now Angular selects the element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 142.38,
          "end": 145.11,
          "en": "by attribute and not by the element itself",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 145.11,
          "end": 147.99,
          "en": "because we changed the selector.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 147.99,
          "end": 152.81,
          "en": "Another alternative is to select by, and I'm just going to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 152.81,
          "end": 155.37,
          "en": "comment this out so that the code is still there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 155.37,
          "end": 158.52,
          "en": "for reference to select by class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 158.52,
          "end": 161.4,
          "en": "So if a dot at the beginning, app servers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 161.4,
          "end": 164.04,
          "en": "again, just like in css.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 164.04,
          "end": 168.03,
          "en": "So here we can now select by class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 168.03,
          "end": 171.84,
          "en": "So let's add a new div here, which has a css class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 171.84,
          "end": 175.32,
          "en": "of app servers, which we of course could now also style.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 175.32,
          "end": 178.56900000000002,
          "en": "But besides that, it's also recognized by Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 178.56900000000002,
          "end": 182.37,
          "en": "as a selector, which is why we still see the app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 182.37,
          "end": 184.348,
          "en": "Now these are all options you have,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 184.348,
          "end": 187.83,
          "en": "as a side note selecting by ID won't work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 187.83,
          "end": 189.547,
          "en": "that's not supported by Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 189.547,
          "end": 192.3,
          "en": "And all those pseudo selectors",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 192.3,
          "end": 195.69,
          "en": "like hover and so on also don't work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 195.69,
          "end": 199.2,
          "en": "And you typically use the elements style here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 199.2,
          "end": 201.69,
          "en": "app servers for components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 201.69,
          "end": 203.7,
          "en": "We will soon learn about directives",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 203.7,
          "end": 205.98,
          "en": "in our feature where this is different.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 205.98,
          "end": 209.82,
          "en": "But for components you typically create your own elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 209.82,
          "end": 213.12,
          "en": "and therefore you don't use that style",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 213.12,
          "end": 216.06,
          "en": "and you don't use the attribute style.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 216.06,
          "end": 219.87,
          "en": "Instead you use app-servers like a element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 219.87,
          "end": 223.32,
          "en": "But it is important to understand that you are not limited",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 223.32,
          "end": 225.48,
          "en": "to this and there might be use cases",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 225.48,
          "end": 227.853,
          "en": "where you want to use a different selector.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
